  "body": "## Highlights\n- Faster installs: a fresh install (no lockfile, 50 packages) is 2.4x faster than v0.38.1 on Linux and macOS, and 2x faster on Windows.\n- Re-running `apm install` with nothing to change is about 3x faster than v0.38.1 at 10 packages and 6-7x faster at 50, on Linux, macOS and Windows. `apm install --frozen` with nothing to change is 2.4-2.9x faster at 10 packages and 4.3-4.9x at 50.\n- Claude instructions: install-only projects keep the 0.37 `.claude/rules/` layout; compiled `AGENTS.md` keeps working (#5394).\n- Safer supply chain: checkouts are verified against their commit objects, cached git config is allow-listed, refs must match an origin branch or tag exactly, and APM's helper tools resolve only from outside the project.\n- Install crash recovery: an interrupted install restores the files it changed, or reports the ones it cannot restore.\n- Community: thanks to @AndresDvst (#3737), @anrouxel (#4807), @Yshuro (#5243) and @MohammedAlkindi (#4576, which returns in 0.40 with a safety ceiling), and to @Melivo for reporting #5415.\n\n## Fixed\n- Helper tools such as git installed under your home directory are found when you run APM outside a project, for example `apm install -g` from your home directory (#5468, #5470).\n\n## Breaking changes and upgrade notes\nSee the \"Breaking changes and upgrade notes\" section of CHANGELOG (11 entries). The most likely to affect you:\n- **Blocking org policy now refuses installs** that violate `manifest.scripts: deny`, `unmanaged_files.action: deny` or `dependencies.max_depth`; the error names the field to fix (#4853).\n- Exact dependency refs (a ref must name an origin branch or tag exactly).\n- Transitive MCP servers need an `mcp.allow` entry under any org policy unless `mcp.trust_transitive: true`.\n- A self-defined transitive MCP server you trusted in 0.38 with `--trust-transitive-mcp` is parked and removed on your first plain 0.39 install. To keep it, run `apm approve <pkg>` and then `apm install` again; if your org policy blocks transitive servers not listed in `mcp.allow`, the policy owner must also add it there.\n- Helper tools (git, az, npm) resolve only from PATH directories outside the project.\n\n### Claude instructions (since 0.38.0)\n<OPS holds relnote-5343.md; keep that section verbatim.>\n\n## Known issues\n- In a monorepo, a package that depends on a sibling package by local path records that sibling's absolute path in `apm.lock.yaml`, so clones at different paths produce different lockfiles and the path can include your user name. Check `apm.lock.yaml` for absolute paths before you commit it. A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#5418).\n- On Windows, `apm uninstall` can exit 1 if another process (an editor or an antivirus scan) holds a deployed file open. Close it and run `apm uninstall` again. A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#5441).\n- The unmanaged-files policy gate does not yet count the MCP, hook and LSP configuration files that install creates or edits (for example `.mcp.json`, Claude hook settings, `.github/lsp.json`). A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#4956).\n- `apm update` does not pick up content changes in a local dependency (`./path`); run `apm install` to redeploy it. A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#5463).\n- Declaring the same local directory twice with different spellings (`./vendor/a` and `./vendor/a/`) records two lock rows; declare each local dependency once. A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#5455).\n- If `apm install <new-package>` is killed abruptly (for example by SIGKILL or power loss), `apm.yml` can list the package without a lock row and `apm install --frozen` then fails; run a plain `apm install` to repair it. A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#5454).\n- A local dependency diamond whose parents spell one directory with different case or Unicode normalization at different depths can make `apm install --frozen` fail; spell local paths consistently. A fix is planned for 0.40.0 (#5457).\n",
